  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/commit-snapshots/a9e1d2ad5a7569010c685b271965ae4a3a34a64b/#refresh\r\n\r\n> 16\\.10 \\`Refresh\\`\r\n> This section describes a header for registration in the Permanent Message Header Field Registry\\. \\[RFC3864\\]\r\n> \r\n> Header field name:​\r\n> Refresh\r\n> Applicable protocol:​\r\n> http\r\n> Status:​\r\n> standard\r\n> Author/Change controller:​\r\n> WHATWG\r\n> Specification document\\(s\\):​\r\n> This document is the relevant specification\\.\r\n> Related information:​\r\n> None\\.\r\n\r\nIt would be helpful to link to the part of the spec that defines this header. https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsing-the-web.html#initialise-the-document-object\r\n\r\nMaybe it could also say something about what the header does.",
